-- Weekly time attack, auto-picked (the owner, 2026-11-11: "time attacks should be autogenerated in any area we have users
-- weekly, not based on user stages. They should be the best loops roads in the area chosen at random. Possibly small
-- loops"). The week's circuit is no longer a member's stage: the first phone in an area that week builds a small loop over
-- the area's best roads with Vetta's own router, from a starting point picked at random for that week and area (the same
-- for every phone), and the server keeps the first one that checks out. The loop lives on its ta_weeks row, ta_weeks
-- .segment_id is its id ("ta-" + uuid), what entrants' copies carry as origin_id. `tries` counts loops a moderator took
-- down this week, so the next one is picked from a different start. Nobody's name is on a loop: who built it isn't kept.
-- ta_pool (members' stages put up) is no longer read, it stays for now and goes in a later clean-up. Additive only.
-- Undo: the columns stay unread by the old code (it joins segments by segment_id, a loop's id has no segment, so its week
-- shows no circuit) and can be dropped with ALTER TABLE ta_weeks DROP COLUMN for each.
ALTER TABLE ta_weeks ADD COLUMN name TEXT;
ALTER TABLE ta_weeks ADD COLUMN length_m REAL;
-- geom: JSON [[lat, lon], ...], starting and ending at the start. removed: 1 when a moderator took this week's loop down.
ALTER TABLE ta_weeks ADD COLUMN geom TEXT;
ALTER TABLE ta_weeks ADD COLUMN tries INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
ALTER TABLE ta_weeks ADD COLUMN removed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
